  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Pair: {写|うつ}す (transitive, to copy/photograph).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {写真|しゃしん}に{写|うつ}る (appear in a photo)\n- きれいに{写|うつ}る (come out nicely)\n- よく{写|うつ}る (come out well)\n- {写|うつ}っている (is shown/captured in)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {写|うつ}る: to be photographed, to be copied\n- {映|うつ}る: to be reflected, to be projected on screen\n- {移|うつ}る: to move, to transfer\n\n{写|うつ}る focuses on photographic and copy reproduction, while {映|うつ}る is about reflections and on-screen images.",
